// Planted fixture for app/test_suppose.mjs (18 Oct 2026), in the fixture-maker's own words. Three
// actors carry a chain, one state is carried by two of them, and the outcome needs two starting
// states together: so "suppose this actor does nothing" stops what that actor alone carries and
// leaves the shared state standing, and "what the starting states do" finds a conjunction.
===
title: "Planted -- who carries the chain"
reconstruction:
    generated: true
mechanism:
    question: "What brings smaller classes about?"
    levels: [system, school]
    actors:
        ministry: {label: "The ministry", level: system}
        heads:    {label: "Head teachers", level: school}
        unions:   {label: "The unions", level: school}
    states:
        money:    {label: "The ministry funds more posts", actor: ministry, role: condition}
        deal:     {label: "A staffing agreement", actor: [heads, unions], role: condition}
        hire:     {label: "Schools hire teachers", actor: heads}
        smaller:  {label: "Classes are smaller", actor: heads, role: outcome}
===

[Classes will shrink]: Classes will become smaller.

[Funded posts get filled]: Where the ministry funds posts and a staffing agreement is in place, schools hire.
    {fidelity: "compression", causes: {from: money, to: hire, sign: "+", basis: asserted, jointly: [deal]}}
    +> [Classes will shrink]

[Hiring shrinks classes]: More teachers make classes smaller.
    {fidelity: "compression", causes: {from: hire, to: smaller, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}
    +> [Classes will shrink]
